{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1000", "sample_idx": 16, "model_name": "google/gemma-3n-e4b-it", "content": "Raymond III Count of Tripoli ruled the County of Tripoli from 1154 until his death in 1199. He was a significant figure in the Crusades a powerful and influential ruler navigating complex political landscapes and military challenges. His reign saw both expansion and consolidation of Tripoli's territory and influence within the Levant.\n\n*Early Life and Ascension* Raymond was born around 1110 the son of Raymond II Count of Tripoli and Countess Sophia of Armenia. He inherited the County of Tripoli upon his father's death in 1154. His early years were marked by securing his position against internal rivals and external threats particularly from Muslim forces. He faced challenges from emirs and sultans who sought to reclaim the territory lost to the Crusaders. Raymond skillfully employed diplomacy and military strength to maintain control.\n\nRaymond III’s reign was characterized by a proactive foreign policy. He forged alliances with other Crusader states like Antioch and Jerusalem seeking mutual defense and strategic advantage. He also engaged in frequent military campaigns against the Ayyubid dynasty a rising power in the region. These campaigns aimed to protect Tripoli's borders and secure its economic interests. He actively participated in Crusades contributing troops and resources to the broader effort to recapture Jerusalem. His military leadership was often decisive securing victories and repelling enemy incursions.\n\n*Political and Economic Policies* Raymond III implemented policies to strengthen Tripoli's economy and infrastructure. He fostered trade relations with various Mediterranean ports promoting economic prosperity within the county. He invested in fortifications bolstering Tripoli's defenses against potential attacks. He also maintained a strong administrative system ensuring efficient governance and justice. His court became a center of culture and learning attracting scholars and artists. He skillfully balanced the needs of his vassals and the demands of the crown ensuring stability and loyalty.\n\n*Military Campaigns and Conflicts* Raymond III engaged in numerous military campaigns throughout his reign. He fought against Saladin and other Ayyubid rulers in several battles. He also dealt with internal rebellions and external threats from various Muslim factions. His military successes helped to maintain Tripoli's independence and protect its territory. He often relied on a combination of defensive fortifications and offensive campaigns to achieve his goals. His military strategies were adaptable and effective enabling him to overcome challenging circumstances. He died in 1199 leaving behind a legacy of strong leadership and successful governance. His reign significantly shaped the history of the County of Tripoli.\n", "logprobs": [{"token": "Raymond", "logprob": -0.0021344278939068317}, {"token": "▁III", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": "▁Count", "logprob": -2.50339189733495e-06}, {"token": "▁of", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": "▁Tripoli", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": "▁ruled", "logprob": -0.2371193766593933}, {"token": "▁the", "logprob": -0.20648594200611115}, {"token": "▁County", "logprob": -0.054002758115530014}, {"token": "▁of", "logprob": -3.576278118089249e-07}, {"token": "▁Tripoli", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": "▁from", "logprob": -0.00023135847004596144}, {"token": "▁", "logprob": -2.5987286790041253e-05}, {"token": "1", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": "1", "logprob": -8.583032467868179e-06}, {"token": "5", "logprob": -2.2649508537142538e-05}, {"token": "4", "logprob": -0.0034172493033111095}, {"token": "▁until", "logprob": -0.03166874870657921}, {"token": "▁his", "logprob": -0.00028081765049137175}, {"token": "▁death", "logprob": -1.4305012882687151e-05}, {"token": "▁in", "logprob": -5.1377883210079744e-05}, {"token": "▁", "logprob": -0.0001646144810365513}, {"token": "1", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": "1", "lo